-- title:
--   Worst-case bound on the run time of the all-edges host at the middle dimension after the choice of the prime
-- statement:
--   Let $x$ be an Exact Triangle instance with $n$ vertices per part and weight bound $U$ satisfying the precondition of the host in a memory $\mu$ with free pointer $f$, let $16\le D\le n$ and $1\le g\le\lfloor\sqrt D\rfloor$, and let $T_n$ be any time function of the Lop-AE-SparseTri solver. Write $s=\lfloor\sqrt D\rfloor$, $q=\lceil s/g\rceil$ and $D_{\mathrm m}=qs$. Then the time of the run after the choice of the prime, for the host data with inner dimension $D_{\mathrm m}$, is bounded by an expression that no longer depends on the prime or on the instance data:
--   $$t_{\mathrm{run}}\le t_{\mathrm{dbl}}(\beta)+3\,t_{\mathrm{res}}(n^2,\beta)+t_{\mathrm{classes}}(n,s)+t_{\mathrm{chunks}}(s,4ng)+B(T_n,n,U,D,g)+80,\qquad\beta=\mathrm{bitLen}(U),$$
--   where the loop bound is
--   $$B=4ng\Big(t_{\mathrm{writes}}(n,D,q)+\sup T_n\big(n,D_{\mathrm m},\lfloor n^2/\sqrt D\rfloor\big)+t_{\mathrm{answers}}\big(\lfloor n^2/\sqrt D\rfloor\big)\Big)+\big(t_{\mathrm{scan}}(q)+20\big)\big(F(n,U,D)+n^2\big)+14 .$$
--   Here $\sup T_n(n,D_{\mathrm m},w)$ is the largest time of the solver on $n$ vertices, inner dimension $D_{\mathrm m}$ and at most $w$ query pairs, and $F(n,U,D)=\lfloor c_F\,\kappa(n,U)\,n^3\log n/\sqrt D\rfloor$ is the bound on the false positives of the hashing (with $\kappa(n,U)=\max(1,\log U/\log n)$ and $c_F$ the constant of the hashing lemma).
--
--   The bound uses that the prime is at most $\sqrt D$, that there are at most $4ng$ instances and chunks, that each instance has inner dimension $D_{\mathrm m}\le D$ and at most $\lfloor n^2/\sqrt D\rfloor$ query pairs, and that the scans are at most the false positives plus the $n^2$ pairs (each pair is scanned to success at most once). It is the step from the time of one run to the bound of Theorem 17 at the middle dimension.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is `aeRunTime Tn (midHostData x D g) x.U ≤ tDblTable (bitLen x.U) + 3 * tResidues (x.n * x.n) (bitLen x.U) + tClasses x.n (Nat.sqrt D) + tChunks (Nat.sqrt D) (4 * x.n * g) + midLoopBound Tn x.n x.U D g + 80`, under `x.Pre μ fr` and `BigCase x.n D g`; all quantities are natural numbers.
